## Summary

• Fixed the MemoryRouter mock export issue in `src/pages/__tests__/Index.recentLeadsNavigation.test.tsx` by changing from:
  ```typescript
  vi.mock('react-router-dom', () => ({
    ...import('react-router-dom'),
    useNavigate: () => mockNavigate,
  }));
  ```
  to:
  ```typescript
  vi.mock('react-router-dom', async () => {
    const actual = await vi.importActual<typeof import('react-router-dom')>('react-router-dom');
    return { ...actual, useNavigate: () => mockNavigate };
  });
  ```

• Eliminated all "No 'MemoryRouter' export is defined on the 'react-router-dom' mock" errors from the test suite

• Reduced test failures from 39 to 38 (1 test fixed by the MemoryRouter mock correction)

• Verified that no other files have the MemoryRouter import + incomplete mock pattern that would cause export errors

